    "required_age": 0,
    "is_free": false,
    "detailed_description": "<h2 class=\"bb_tag\">It Could Have Been Me</h2><div class=\"bb_img_ctn\"><img class=\"bb_img\" src=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/803840/extras/d987c3458b2156fcb43fe021b399fafb.avif?t=1558250354\" /></div><br>An experience about an unaccompanied youth's journey from Afghanistan to Sweden, and a tribute to these youngster who risk their lives to create a better future for themselves.<br><br><ul class=\"bb_ul\"><li>26 documentary stories from unaccompanied youths from Afghanistan, as well as activists and employees at the Swedish Migration Agency<br></li><li>5 surreal worlds: the mountains, the tunnel, the train station, the caves, and the heavens<br></li><li>Rap from Emilia Carapic (Bac Nini), based on the dreams of the newly arrived<br></li><li>Travel in VR using Oculus Touch controllers and the latest Oculus Rift<br></li><li>Estimated playtime: 20 minutes per journey. Play multiples to experience new stories<br></li><li>Surreal and realistic like life itself, with both artistic and documentary elements.<br></li><li>Dialogue available in both English and Swedish, depending on choices made in the tutorial</li></ul><br><div class=\"bb_img_ctn\"><img class=\"bb_img\" src=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/803840/extras/a83d266e559723638dd20ed45e852bdc.avif?t=1558250354\" /></div><br><i>It could have been me, it could have been you, who had been forced to make this journey.</i>",
    "about_the_game": "<h2 class=\"bb_tag\">It Could Have Been Me</h2><div class=\"bb_img_ctn\"><img class=\"bb_img\" src=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/803840/extras/d987c3458b2156fcb43fe021b399fafb.avif?t=1558250354\" /></div><br>An experience about an unaccompanied youth's journey from Afghanistan to Sweden, and a tribute to these youngster who risk their lives to create a better future for themselves.<br><br><ul class=\"bb_ul\"><li>26 documentary stories from unaccompanied youths from Afghanistan, as well as activists and employees at the Swedish Migration Agency<br></li><li>5 surreal worlds: the mountains, the tunnel, the train station, the caves, and the heavens<br></li><li>Rap from Emilia Carapic (Bac Nini), based on the dreams of the newly arrived<br></li><li>Travel in VR using Oculus Touch controllers and the latest Oculus Rift<br></li><li>Estimated playtime: 20 minutes per journey. Play multiples to experience new stories<br></li><li>Surreal and realistic like life itself, with both artistic and documentary elements.<br></li><li>Dialogue available in both English and Swedish, depending on choices made in the tutorial</li></ul><br><div class=\"bb_img_ctn\"><img class=\"bb_img\" src=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/803840/extras/a83d266e559723638dd20ed45e852bdc.avif?t=1558250354\" /></div><br><i>It could have been me, it could have been you, who had been forced to make this journey.</i>",
    "short_description": "A journey from Afganistan to Sweden. Experience 26 documentary stories and 5 surreal worlds in VR. Rap from Emilia Carapic (Bac Nini)Voices from experiencers during the Night of Culture in Lund, where over 80 people tried the experience:&quot;The coolest thing I've seen!",
    "reviews": "\u201cThe coolest thing I've seen!\u201d<br />\r\n10 year old boy<br />\r\n<br />\r\n\u201cI don't want it to end\u201d<br />\r\n75 year old lady<br />\r\n<br />\r\n\u201cFantastic\u201d<br />\r\n45 year old woman<br />\r\n",
